ANNOTATION: "SEP-XBAR-TARGET-TIED: each target port carries only beats from the initiators that Connectivity (sep_local_axi_xbar_pkg.sv:140-146) lets reach it, held in axi_mux spill registers that reset to 0 and load only on a valid handshake (vendor/pulp-platform/common_cells/upstream/src/spill_register_flushable.sv:45-47,78; LatencyMode CUT_ALL_PORTS at sep_local_axi_xbar_pkg.sv:126). axi_mux prepends the 3-bit initiator index above the 3-bit initiator ID (axi_id_prepend.sv:92-93). A listed bit is 0 in every address of the target's AddrMap rules (sep_local_axi_xbar.sv:96-206, extents from hw/sys/sep/regs/gen/sv/sep_addrmap_pkg.sv:17-21,234-235), or 0 in the index of every connected initiator, or a field every connected initiator ties to 0 (IFU el2_ifu_mem_ctl.sv:1074-1101; LSU qos/lock/AWATOP/AxUSER[11:4] el2_lsu_bus_buffer.sv:881-907 and sep_cpu.sv:497-507; debug el2_dbg.sv:738-774 and sep_cpu.sv:501-508; DMA axi_lite_to_axi.sv:39-67 and sep_dma_wrap.sv:283-284; ext id[2] axi_id_remap.sv:198-200). SEP_SOURCE_ID is 4'b1111 (sep_pkg.sv:489), so AxUSER[11:4] is 0 for the CPU masters. LSU prot/len/burst are not used as ties because a no_cpu TB force moves them. NOT waived: address bits that are 1 inside a rule (0->1 after the first access, 1->0 only on reset), and every field an integrator-driven initiator (ext) or a free CPU/DMA field can move."
